  "banner": {
    "kind": "info",
    "title_en": "👋 Lessons 8, 9, 10 and 11 are still waiting",
    "body_en": "Whenever you have a few minutes, reply with your answers to Lessons 8 (numbers), 9 (names and ages), 10 and 11 (colors) so I can grade them. No rush. Today we start a new category: animals!",
    "body_py": "Nǐ yǒu kòng de shíhou, qǐng huífù dì-bā, dì-jiǔ, dì-shí hé dì-shíyī kè de dá'àn, wǒ lái pǔfēn. Bù jí. Jīntiān wǒmen kāishǐ xué xīn de zhǔtí: dòngwù!"
  },
  "teach": {
    "intro": {
      "en": "Hi Evan! You've done a lot with colors, so today we move on to animals. You'll learn the word for animal, then cat and dog, plus zhī, the little counting word used for animals. Kids love this topic, so you can try it out on the little ones at home. We'll also warm up some older words that are due for a refresh.",
      "py": "Nǐ hǎo, Evan! Nǐ zài yánsè fāngmiàn yǐjīng xué le hěn duō, suǒyǐ jīntiān wǒmen xué dòngwù. Nǐ huì xué “dòngwù”, “māo” hé “gǒu”, hái yǒu “zhī”, jiùshì shuō dòngwù shí yòng de xiǎo liàngcí. Háizi men dōu xǐhuan zhège zhǔtí, nǐ kěyǐ hé jiā lǐ de xiǎo péngyou liànxí yíxià. Wǒmen yě fùxí yìxiē gāi fùxí de jiù cí."
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "New words"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "animal",
        "py": "dòngwù",
        "note_en": "Both syllables are 4th tone, so they fall: DÒNG-WÙ. Wù at the end is short and sharp.",
        "note_py": "Liǎng gè zì dōu shì dì-sì shēng, dōu wǎng xià jiàng: dòng-wù. Wù zài zuìhòu yòu duǎn yòu zhòng.",
        "listen_url": "l12-dongwu.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "cat",
        "py": "māo",
        "note_en": "1st tone, high and flat, like a long \"mow\" with no bend.",
        "note_py": "Māo shì dì-yī shēng, yòu gāo yòu píng, xiàng yí gè bù zhuǎnwān de “mao”.",
        "listen_url": "l12-mao.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "dog",
        "py": "gǒu",
        "note_en": "3rd tone: dip down and back up, like saying \"go?\" with a little question in your voice.",
        "note_py": "Gǒu shì dì-sān shēng, xiān xià zài shàng, hǎoxiàng wèn “go?” yíyàng.",
        "listen_url": "l12-gou.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "(counter for animals)",
        "py": "zhī",
        "note_en": "Say yì zhī (one animal) or liǎng zhī (two animals) between the number and the animal. It has no English word. It's the same job as gè for people.",
        "note_py": "Zài shùzì hé dòngwù zhōngjiān shuō yì zhī huò liǎng zhī. Yīngyǔ méiyǒu duìyìng de cí. Tā gēn rén de gè zuò yíyàng de shì.",
        "listen_url": "l12-zhi.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "I have a dog.",
        "py": "Wǒ yǒu yì zhī gǒu.",
        "note_en": "Word for word: \"I have one-zhī dog.\" The number yī becomes yì before a 1st tone like zhī. Also, wǒ yǒu is said wó yǒu (3rd + 3rd).",
        "note_py": "Zhè jù huà jiù shì: wǒ yǒu yì zhī gǒu. Yī hòumiàn shì dì-yī shēng de zhī, yào shuō yì. Wǒ yǒu shuō chéng wó yǒu (liǎng gè dì-sān shēng).",
        "listen_url": "l12-wo-you-yi-zhi-gou.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "kind": "pattern",
        "title": "🔑 Pattern: number + zhī + animal",
        "body_en": "For animals, always put a counting word between the number and the animal: yì zhī gǒu, liǎng zhī māo. You already know liǎng gè rén for people. Animals just use zhī.",
        "body_py": "Shuō dòngwù yào zài shùzì hé dòngwù zhōngjiān jiā liàngcí: yì zhī gǒu, liǎng zhī māo. Nǐ yǐjīng zhīdào shuō rén yòng liǎng gè rén. Dòngwù jiù yòng zhī.",
        "pairs": [
          {
            "en": "one cat",
            "py": "yì zhī māo"
          },
          {
            "en": "two dogs",
            "py": "liǎng zhī gǒu"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "kind": "tip",
        "title": "💡 Tip: no plural in Chinese",
        "body_en": "Māo can mean one cat or many cats. The number tells you how many, so you never add an \"s\".",
        "body_py": "Māo kěyǐ shì yì zhī māo, yě kěyǐ shì hěn duō zhī māo. Shùzì gàosu nǐ yǒu jǐ zhī, bú yòng jiā “s”."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Review: due words"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "en": "These words are due for a refresh, and the colors from Lessons 10 and 11 haven't had a first practice yet. Listen, then say each one out loud.",
        "py": "Zhèxiē cí gāi fùxí le, ér dì-shí hé dì-shíyī kè de yánsè hái méiyǒu liànxí guò. Xiān tīng, ránhòu dàshēng shuō."
      },
